+Load returns isolated TOML bytes, one immutable resolved-root snapshot, and an
+isolated current-model Configuration when the selected file exists. It dispatches
+strict closed-table readers for Configuration 1.0.0, 2.0.0, and 3.0.0 from the
+pinned catalog; v1/v2 are translated in memory to v3 without changing their
+source bytes. `EncodeCurrent` validates and emits only Configuration 3.0.0.
+Backend-specific v3 settings require an exact caller-supplied settings validator;
+without one, a `backend_config` entry fails closed rather than accepting an
+arbitrary blob.
+
+A not-yet-created configuration file is accepted only when its parent directory
 exists, and ConfigPresent distinguishes that state from an existing empty
-file. It does not enumerate environment variables, copy ambient credentials,
-interpret unknown AX_* names, mutate roots, create files, parse versioned TOML
-schemas, migrate configuration, advertise doctor/CLI support, or claim a
-runtime capability. Versioned Configuration 1/2/3 decoding and explicit atomic
-migration remain owned by separate implementation tasks. Existing selected
+file. Versioned validation applies the exact defaults, closed members, scalar
+and relational bounds, unique/sorted registries, SSH host-authentication
+refusals, directory disclosure constraints, and v3 TerminalBackend trust/config
+shape from Sections 6 and 17. The supported reader set is tested as a derived
+property of the pinned Configuration catalog, so a new catalog version cannot
